[{:db/id "04750ba1-7d77-5b3e-adbe-fb66cc839d72" :answer/id #uuid "04750ba1-7d77-5b3e-adbe-fb66cc839d72" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "54\\sqrt{22}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "5d0cc3a7-0b20-5f18-b1bb-75c69ce02711" :answer-field/id #uuid "5d0cc3a7-0b20-5f18-b1bb-75c69ce02711" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/choices ["04750ba1-7d77-5b3e-adbe-fb66cc839d72"] :answer-field/correct "04750ba1-7d77-5b3e-adbe-fb66cc839d72" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "44e31a62-0afc-5503-b1c7-497ce942e02a" :question/id #uuid "44e31a62-0afc-5503-b1c7-497ce942e02a" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\\iint_S(x-y)\\,\\text{d}S,$$\n\nwhere $r(u,v)=⟨3u+v,\\,3u-v,\\,3v⟩$ for $0\\le u\\le 2$ and $0\\le v\\le 3.$\n\n*Hint: $‖r_u′\\times r_v′‖=3\\sqrt{22}.$*\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice that we are told that the norm of the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖=3\\sqrt{22}.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$f(r(u,v))=(3u+v)-(3u-v)=2v.$$\n\nTherefore, our surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\iint_S(x-y)\\,\\text{d}S&=\\iint_D f(r(u,v))‖r_u′\\times r_v′‖\\,\\text{d}A\\\\&=3\\sqrt{22}\\iint_D 2v\\,\\text{d}A\\\\&=3\\sqrt{22}\\int_0^{3}2v\\,\\text{d}v\\cdot\\int_0^{2}1\\,\\text{d}u\\\\&=3\\sqrt{22}[v^{2}]_0^{3}[u]_0^{2}\\\\&=3\\sqrt{22}(9-0)(2-0)\\\\&=54\\sqrt{22}.\\end{aligned}$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["5d0cc3a7-0b20-5f18-b1bb-75c69ce02711"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "dac57afd-cb85-5e46-a6c1-819e0317af41" :answer/id #uuid "dac57afd-cb85-5e46-a6c1-819e0317af41" :answer/type